TITLE:: ViewQtKey
SUMMARY:: Qt Key enum values for the key argument of LINK::Classes/View:: keyboard actions.
CATEGORIES:: GUI
RELATED:: Classes/ViewKeyModifier, Classes/ViewKeycode, Classes/ViewUnicode, Classes/SequencerKeyRouter

DESCRIPTION::
The fifth argument to LINK::Classes/View:: CODE::keyDownAction:: / CODE::keyUpAction:: is the Qt CODE::Key_:: enum integer (the same namespace as LINK::Classes/QKey:: arrow constants, but letter keys use ASCII code points).

Use these named constants instead of raw integers when matching or synthesizing key events.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: control
The Control modifier key itself (key-up/key-down for the modifier, not “Ctrl held”).

METHOD:: enter
Qt Enter (typically keypad).

METHOD:: left
Left arrow.

METHOD:: m
Letter M (ASCII CODE::77::).

METHOD:: return
Qt Return / main Enter key.

METHOD:: right
Right arrow.
